# `bazel run --@rules_go//go/toolchain:sdk_name=go_civisibility_sdk \
#     //test/new-e2e/tests:install_test_binaries -- --destdir=<dir>`
# builds and installs every e2e test binary, CI Visibility-instrumented via
# //bazel/rules/go_civisibility's patched toolchain, replacing the
# ThreadPoolExecutor-driven loop in tasks/new_e2e_tests.py's build_binaries
# with Bazel's own scheduling, caching, and atomic build-then-install.
#
# Every native `go_test` target explicitly tagged "civisibility" is listed
# below, since pkg_files cannot glob across packages. The tag is applied by
# hand to each genuine e2e suite (via buildozer, not computed by a macro or
# Gazelle from its deps: Bazel's own guidance discourages deriving labels or
# tags from other attributes, since it makes the BUILD graph's behavior
# unpredictable from reading the file alone). test/new-e2e/tests also holds
# plain unit tests for shared helper packages (e.g. agent-platform/common's
# bound-port) that never import test/e2e-framework/testing/e2e, so they
# don't get the tag and fail to link if built against the patched stdlib:
# its `//go:linkname` calls into dd-trace-go's civisibility internals only
# resolve if the binary also imports that package somewhere. Untag a target
# if it stops needing this, tag a new one when it starts. Regenerate the
# list below (not the tagging itself) with:
#
#     bazel query 'kind(go_test, attr(tags, "\bcivisibility\b", //test/new-e2e/tests/...))' --output=label
#
# Destination names follow the same convention tasks/new_e2e_tests.py's
# build_binaries already uses (pkg.replace("/", "-") + ".test"), so two
# different-package binaries with the same base target name (e.g. two
# "file-tailing" packages) do not collide.
_TEST_BINARIES = {
    "//test/new-e2e/tests/agent-configuration:agent-configuration_test": "tests-agent-configuration.test",
